SHOWER DATA

The meteor shower facts this package carries are read from the IAU Meteor Data
Center's list of established showers:

  IAU Meteor Data Center (IAU Commission F1, Meteors, Meteorites and
  Interplanetary Dust) — Established meteor showers, V.2.
  https://www.ta3.sk/IAUC22DB/MDC2022/Etc/streamestablisheddata2026.txt

The MDC database is maintained on an unpaid voluntary basis and asks to be
cited. Its requested references are:

  Jenniskens, P.; Jopek, T.J.; Janches, D.; Hajdukova, M.; Kokhirova,
  G.I.; Rudawska, R.; 2020, Planetary and Space Science, Vol. 182, article
  id. 104821

  Jopek, T.J.; Kanuchova, Z.; 2017, Planetary and Space Science, Vol. 143,
  p. 3-6

  Jopek, T.J.; Kanuchova, Z.; 2014, in The Meteoroids 2013, Proceedings of
  the Astronomical Conference, A.M. University Press, p. 353-364

  Jopek, T.J.; Jenniskens, P.M.; 2011, in Meteoroids: The Smallest Solar
  System Bodies, NASA/CP-2011-216469, p. 7-13

The authors' names carry diacritics that are preserved exactly in
src/meteor_mcp/data/SOURCE.json and in what meteor_source_info returns; they
are transliterated here only because this file is plain ASCII.

This package does not redistribute the MDC's file. It records the file's URL,
retrieval date and SHA-256, and holds the facts read from it. The shower
numbers, codes, names and radiants are the MDC's and are not claimed.

